.TH SUDOSRV 8 "2026-08-17" "sudosrv" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
sudosrv \- sudo I/O log server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudosrv
.RB [ \-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-log-level
.IR level ]
.RB [ \-validate ]
.RB [ \-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.RB [ \-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sudosrv
receives I/O logs from
.BR sudo (8)
clients over the sudo_logsrv protocol and is a drop-in alternative to sudo's
own
.BR sudo_logsrvd (8).
It accepts connections from sudo 1.9.0 and newer, over plain TCP, TLS, or both
at once.
.PP
It runs in one of two modes, selected by
.I server.mode
in the configuration file.
In
.B local
mode it writes sudoreplay-compatible session transcripts under
.IR local_storage.log_directory .
In
.B relay
mode it caches each session on disk and forwards it to an upstream server,
retrying with exponential backoff, so an upstream outage costs no audit records.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Configuration file to read. Default:
.IR /etc/sudosrv/config.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-log-level " level"
Operational log level for the daemon's own logging:
.BR debug ", " info ", " warn ", or " error .
Overrides
.I server.server_operational_log_level
in the configuration file. This is the daemon's diagnostic log, distinct from
the sudo event log and from the session transcripts.
.TP
.B \-validate
Parse and validate the configuration, report any problem, and exit without
binding a socket. Exits 0 when the configuration is usable.
.TP
.B \-dry-run
Validate the configuration and report what the daemon would do, without
starting it.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the configuration and apply changes to the listen addresses and to
every TLS setting without dropping established connections. Certificates
renewed in place need no signal at all; the key pair is re-read per handshake.
Sent by
.B systemctl reload sudosrv
and by the shipped logrotate stanza.
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Shut down gracefully: stop accepting new connections, let sessions in flight
finish, and flush what is pending.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General failure.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Server error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sudosrv/config.yaml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/log/sudosrv
Session transcripts in local mode.
.TP
.I /var/spool/sudosrv-cache
Undelivered session journals in relay mode. Do not point
.BR logrotate (8)
at this directory: rotating a journal renames it out of reach of the flush and
recovery code, which destroys an undelivered session permanently.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR logsh (8),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR sudoreplay (8),
.BR sudo_logsrvd (8),
.BR sudoers (5)
